entityDescription:
Forestry France is the leading independent forestry expertise and management company in France. For over 100 years, the company has supported public and private landowners in valuing and preserving their natural heritage. Forestry France supports the resilience of territories through the sustainable management of forests, tree heritage, agricultural land and infrastructure.
Its activity is organized around 6 complementary business units, reflecting the breadth of its expertise: 
- For&ecirc;t (Forests), its historic core business, dedicated to the management and enhancement of forest estates; 
- Arbre (Trees, urban trees), focused on the management of tree heritage, particularly in urban and peri-urban settings; 
- Infra-r&eacute;seaux (Infrastructure, major networks), which manages vegetation along linear infrastructure (roads, railways, networks) and oversees solar farm projects; 
- Agri (Agriculture, agronomy), covering rural leases, land expertise, and agroforestry; 
- Bureau d'&Eacute;tudes (Studies), providing cross-cutting technical and scientific support; 
- Training center (Qualiopi-certified), which shares this expertise with industry professionals.
This structure allows Forestry France to address the full range of challenges related to natural heritage management, well beyond forestry alone. Internationally, the group operates primarily across Europe through its involvement in Forestry Europe, while remaining open to opportunistic engagements elsewhere.
